    "title": "Weak coupling",
    "narration": "With β near zero each state follows its own observation independently; the shading of the white nodes is noisy and uncorrelated across the grid.",
    "state": {
      "viewLayer": "Full model",
      "coupling": 0.05
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Strong coupling",
    "narration": "Raising β makes neighboring white nodes converge to similar shading — the field becomes smooth — even though the gray observations never change.",
    "state": {
      "viewLayer": "Full model",
      "coupling": 2.6
    }
  }
]

AXIS ANGLES: null — null means the source is a flat 2D figure; pass axisScreenAngles: null to setCameraView for a front-on view.

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "heightFraction": 0.62
}

NOTES: Render in Three.js with an OrthographicCamera plus a custom oblique shear matrix (cabinet projection: x' = x + 0.55·z·cos40°, y' = y + 0.55·z·sin40°) rather than an orbiting camera, so the figure keeps the source's flat oblique read; no orbit interaction is offered. Draw nodes as flat circles (CircleGeometry facing camera) with a separate ring mesh or LineLoop for the heavy black outline so stroke weight stays constant. Edges as Line2/LineMaterial fat lines (uniform ~3px screen width) since thin THREE.Line ignores linewidth. Draw order: edges first, then nodes on top (renderOrder / depthTest false) so circles occlude the lines, matching the line-drawing look. Labels as CSS2DRenderer HTML spans with MathJax-style italic subscripts. Click picking via raycaster on the white circle meshes only; on selection, set non-blanket edges and nodes to opacity 0.15 and stroke the blanket edges in a highlight color (#1f77b4) while keeping the selected node's ring thicker. Toggle animates opacity of the two edge groups (grid edges vs vertical y-links) and the gray node group. Slider recomputes node fill colors each frame from a fixed random seed for the observation values so the pattern is stable while β changes. Flat white background, no lighting needed — use MeshBasicMaterial throughout.

Follow the interaction plan above.

